      <!-- Exercise 3 -->
      <div class="case-header">
        <p class="case-label">EXERCISE 3</p>
        <h2 class="case-title">Update a task's status</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="detail-paragraph">
        The goal is to practice editing <strong>a single field</strong> in Notion. We <strong>only allow editing「狀態」</strong> — the AI can't simultaneously modify the task name, due date, notes, or anything else. This makes edits safer and easier to review.
      </p>

      <h4 class="example-heading">How to do it</h4>
      <p class="detail-paragraph">
        First run <strong>Exercise 1</strong> to list tasks and find the one to update. The tool's response includes a <code>page_id</code> — pass that to the AI for the next step.
      </p>

      <div class="callout-card callout-card--warn">
        <p class="callout-text">
          <strong>You must replace the page_id line in the prompt below yourself.</strong><br/><br/>
          If you don't, the AI very likely <strong>won't come back and ask</strong> — it'll go look the value up itself and proceed. That's exactly what happened in testing: it called <code>list_classroom_tasks</code> on its own, matched by task name, found the <code>page_id</code>, and updated successfully.<br/><br/>
          It guessed right that time. But the tool <strong>only validates the shape of the <code>page_id</code>; it never checks whether that's the row you meant</strong>. If the database holds two tasks with similar names, it may well edit the wrong one — and the reply will look exactly the same.
        </p>
      </div>

      <details class="details-card">
        <summary class="details-card__summary">
          <span class="details-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
          <span class="details-card__title">Prompt example</span>
          <span class="details-card__hint">Click to expand the prompt</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="details-card__body">
          <blockquote class="prompt-example">
            Use the notion-classroom tool to update the「準備閱讀材料摘要」 task's status to「處理中」.<br/><br/>
            page_id: (replace this line with the page_id returned in Exercise 1, formatted like 3b84757f-c450-8002-83dc-f6bf37215b68)<br/><br/>
            Important:<br/>
            1. Update only the status.<br/>
            2. Do not change the task name.<br/>
            3. Do not change the due date.<br/>
            4. After updating, please report the result.
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="details-card">
        <summary class="details-card__summary">
          <span class="details-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
          <span class="details-card__title">Possible response</span>
          <span class="details-card__hint">Click to expand a sample response</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="details-card__body">
          <p class="detail-paragraph">The tool call the model made:</p>
          <pre class="code-block" is:raw><code>update_task_status {"new_status":"處理中","page_id":"3b84757f-c450-8002-83dc-f6bf37215b68"}</code></pre>

          <p class="detail-paragraph">What the tool returned:</p>
          <pre class="code-block" is:raw><code class="lang-json">{
  "ok": true,
  "message": "已更新任務狀態。",
  "page_id": "3b84757f-c450-8002-83dc-f6bf37215b68",
  "new_status": "處理中"
}</code></pre>

          <p class="detail-paragraph">The model's reply:</p>
          <blockquote class="prompt-example">
            Successfully updated the「準備閱讀材料摘要」 task's status to「處理中」.<br/><br/>
            Update result:<br/>
            ・Task name: 準備閱讀材料摘要<br/>
            ・Page ID: 3b84757f-c450-8002-83dc-f6bf37215b68<br/>
            ・New status: 處理中
          </blockquote>

          <h4 class="example-heading">Verify back in Notion</h4>
          <p class="detail-paragraph">
            Check the row in Notion afterwards — only the status should have moved:
          </p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Status <strong>changed to「處理中」</strong></li>
            <li>Task name <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
            <li>Category <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
            <li>Priority <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
            <li>Due date 2026-09-25 <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
            <li>Source <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
            <li>Notes <strong>unchanged</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <div class="callout-card">
        <p class="callout-text">
          This exercise makes a few things clear:<br/>
          ✓ The AI can modify data<br/>
          ✓ But <strong>don't let it modify everything from day one</strong><br/>
          ✓ The smaller the edit surface, the easier to review and the safer to ship
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Exercise 4 -->
      <div class="case-header">
        <p class="case-label">EXERCISE 4</p>
        <h2 class="case-title">Organize first, then create the Notion task</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="detail-paragraph">
        The goal is to plug in the "<strong>workflow</strong>" idea from earlier pages. The AI doesn't just call a single tool — it can <strong>organize the text first, then create the Notion task</strong>. The constraints stay in place:
      </p>

      <ol class="numbered-list">
        <li><span class="numbered-list__num">1</span><span class="numbered-list__text">First, <strong>organize the task content</strong></span></li>
        <li><span class="numbered-list__num">2</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Confirm <strong>whether the fields are sufficient</strong></span></li>
        <li><span class="numbered-list__num">3</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Then <strong>create the Notion task</strong></span></li>
        <li><span class="numbered-list__num">4</span><span class="numbered-list__text">If <strong>data is missing</strong>, don't force the creation</span></li>
      </ol>

      <details class="details-card">
        <summary class="details-card__summary">
          <span class="details-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
          <span class="details-card__title">Prompt example</span>
          <span class="details-card__hint">Click to expand the prompt</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="details-card__body">
          <blockquote class="prompt-example">
            Based on the text below, decide whether it's appropriate to create a Notion classroom task.<br/><br/>
            Text:<br/>
            "Next week, remind participants to attend their registered session and ask people who left the diet field blank to fill it in."<br/><br/>
            Please first organize into these fields:<br/>
            1. Task name<br/>
            2. Category<br/>
            3. Priority<br/>
            4. Due date<br/>
            5. Source<br/>
            6. Notes<br/><br/>
            If the due date is unclear, don't guess.<br/>
            Reply with "Missing due date — needs human verification" and don't create the Notion task.
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="details-card">
        <summary class="details-card__summary">
          <span class="details-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
          <span class="details-card__title">Possible response</span>
          <span class="details-card__hint">Click to expand a sample response</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="details-card__body">
          <div class="callout-card">
            <p class="callout-text">
              This one made <strong>no call to <code>create_classroom_task</code></strong> — the Notion database stayed at five rows and gained nothing.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="detail-paragraph">The model's reply:</p>
          <ol class="numbered-list">
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">1</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Task name: 提醒參加者依報名場次出席並補填飲食需求資料</span></li>
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">2</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Category: 行政事項</span></li>
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">3</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Priority: 中</span></li>
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">4</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Due date: unclear</span></li>
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">5</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Source: 報告與出席注意事項</span></li>
            <li><span class="numbered-list__num">6</span><span class="numbered-list__text">Notes: 需提醒參加者依照報告場次出席，並請飲食需求未填的人補填資料。</span></li>
          </ol>

          <div class="callout-card callout-card--warn">
            <p class="callout-text">
              Missing due date — needs human verification
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <figure class="figure">
        <img
          class="figure__img"
          src="/learning/agent/Notion課堂任務管理練習後.png"
          alt="The 課堂任務管理 database after all four exercises, now holding five rows, with 準備閱讀材料摘要 set to 處理中 and 整理下次課程的練習指令 as the last row"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="figure__caption">Figure 10. The database after all four exercises. Compared with Figure 4: the extra fifth row is 「整理下次課程的練習指令」 from Exercise 2, 「準備閱讀材料摘要」 moved from 待確認 to 處理中 in Exercise 3, and Exercise 4 added nothing at all.</figcaption>
